<h2 id="fact-check-notes">Fact-Check Notes</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>3-2-1 backup rule</strong>: Industry best practice (3 copies, 2 different media, 1 offsite). ✅ Verified</li>
<li><strong>ISO 22301</strong>: International standard for business continuity management systems. ✅ Verified</li>
<li><strong>NIST SP 800-34</strong>: NIST Contingency Planning Guide for Federal Information Systems. ✅ Verified</li>
<li><strong>RTO/RPO definitions</strong>: Recovery Time Objective (max tolerable downtime) and Recovery Point Objective (max tolerable data loss) — industry-standard DR metrics. ✅ Verified</li>
<li><strong>Immutable backups</strong>: WORM (Write Once Read Many) storage for ransomware protection — recommended by NIST, CIS, and backup vendor best practices. ✅ Verified</li>
<li><strong>Veeam, Commvault</strong>: Leading enterprise backup solution vendors. ✅ Verified</li>
<li><strong>Hot/Warm/Cold DR sites</strong>: Standard industry classification for disaster recovery site types. ✅ Verified</li>
</ul>
